  recipeId: power
  concept: 'Authored objective: Commission all four VRM phases.

    Authored requirement:
    Verify protected input, both auxiliary rails, four phase outputs and stable VCORE
    at 2 A.

    General teaching principle: Electrical measurements are differences
    or flows that require a correct reference, operating condition and fresh solver
    evidence.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this
    objective is complete.'
  analogy: A pressure gauge needs a reference; a voltage measurement likewise depends
    on its defined points.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An expected rail or current is not a measured rail or current until
    the live circuit evidence confirms it.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Commission all four VRM phases\u2019, which
    component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should
    you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Commission all four VRM phases\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 103, perform the objective \u2018Commission all four VRM phases\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Verify protected
    input, both auxiliary rails, four phase outputs and stable VCORE at 2 A.\nThe
    mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial does not grade your answer."
  guidedOnly: 1
